---
export const title = 'The catalog and its schema';
export const order = 400;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The catalog is generated from the component manifest and a hand-kept allow-list
  (<code>components/bin/generative-catalog/allow-list.mjs</code>): each allowed prop gets its JSON
  kind, its enum values and its description from the component's own documentation, so the schema
  follows the components. A test fails when the committed catalog is out of date or allows a prop
  that could navigate or load an address.
</p>
<p>
  <code>generativeViewSchema()</code>, exported by the package and the loader, returns the catalog as
  a JSON Schema. Give it to the model service as the answer's structured-output schema, or describe it
  in the prompt; the view checks every answer against the same catalog either way.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-json-viewer id='generative-schema' root-label='generativeViewSchema()' expand-depth='2' style='inline-size: 100%; max-block-size: 28rem; overflow: auto;'></wc-json-viewer>
  <script type='module'>
    const script = document.querySelector('script[src*="loader"][type="module"]');
    if (script) {
      const { generativeViewSchema } = await import(script.src);
      document.querySelector('#generative-schema').value = generativeViewSchema();
    }
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>When AI is off</h3>
<p>
  The view renders nothing, like every marker of the assistant. A page that shows generated answers
  must also work without them: the list, the report and the record are still there.
</p>
